# Python build output and the caches the tools leave behind. Anything here
# that grows a virtual environment keeps it local, so the environment
# directories are covered once for the whole repository rather than per tool.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage

# Editors.
.idea/
.vscode/

# Windows shell leavings. Explorer writes both into any directory it is asked
# to display a certain way, and this is a repository whose common case is
# somebody on Windows opening a tool's folder to read it.
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Agent tooling scratch. A worktree is a checkout of this repository living
# inside it, which git would otherwise try to record as a nested repo, and
# settings.local.json is per-user. A shared .claude/settings.json is
# deliberately not ignored, so one can still be committed if ever wanted.
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/settings.local.json

# The agent instructions live in AGENTS.md, which is committed and is what
# every agent reads. CLAUDE.md is only the one-line pointer at it that Claude
# Code looks for, which is per-user scaffolding rather than part of the
# project, so it stays out of the repository.
CLAUDE.md
